{
  "rationale": "Use a small plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration policy in compact deterministic specifications. Clear sensing strongly biases to forward motion, with a brief random-walk diversification layer to avoid overly long straight runs. Obstacle events always force entry into recovery states; front obstacles use a one-shot backward escape before turning, while side obstacles use directed turns away from the blocked side. Commit/recovery states self-loop on path_clear so the intended pulse is not preempted, but safety-critical obstacle events can redirect recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion capability in plant automata",
    "Use one main policy specification plus a small alternation specification to inject occasional random_walk during clear exploration",
    "Make obstacle handling conservative and one-shot, with rapid return to forward exploration when path_clear is observed",
    "Use consistent side-dependent turning: obstacle_left -> rotate_clockwise, obstacle_right -> rotate_counterclockwise"
  ],
